# tools/d/dated_path_repoint_witness.rish -- the repointer's safety rule, proven on metal.
#
# WHY THIS RUNG. tools/fixtures/dated_path_repoint_scan.sh EDITS FILES, and its whole safety rests
# on one rule: a file whose own basename carries a one-clock stamp is dated testimony and is never
# written to. That rule is what keeps a fold from quietly rewriting thousands of session logs and
# counsel notes -- the very breach of accrete-never-break the mark law exists to avoid. A rule
# that has never been tested is a rule nobody has kept, so it is tested here on a tree whose right
# answers are known before the tool runs.
#
# WHAT IS PROVEN. Four files, four known answers, all on metal:
#   a living file citing a folded path IS repointed;
#   a DATED-NAMED file citing the very same path is left byte-identical;
#   a file already citing the folded path is not double-folded;
#   a file citing a dated path that never folded is left alone.
# And a second apply changes nothing, so the pass is idempotent rather than merely correct once.
#
# WHAT IS NOT PROVEN. This proves the rule the tool follows; it does not prove that repointing was
# the right call for any particular room. That judgement is the mark law's, and it is a word.
#
# Season: the Standfast restrategizing of `20260821`, arc one -- the mark and the path.
# Kin: .claude/rules/stamp-and-name.md - tools/d/dated_path_witness.rish - tools/r/room_bound_witness.rish
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/d/dated_path_repoint_witness.rish

say "repoint: Language EN -- a tool that edits files earns trust only where it refuses to. This proves the repointer rewrites living code and leaves every dated artifact byte-identical."
say "repoint: Style Radiant -- one claim, four cases, and idempotence. The rule is that a dated basename is testimony; the proof is a tree built to catch the rule breaking."
say "repoint: Lens TAME -- the control's answers are known before the tool runs, so the check does not depend on the thing it is checking."

let control = run ["sh" "tools/fixtures/dated_path_repoint_control.sh"]
assert control.ok else "repoint: the control tree must build and the repointer must run over it"
say control.out
assert control.out contains "repointed_living=1" else "repoint: a living file citing a folded path must be repointed"
assert control.out contains "untouched_testimony=1" else "repoint: a DATED-NAMED file must be left byte-identical -- this is the rule the whole tool rests on"
assert control.out contains "untouched_already=1" else "repoint: a path already folded must not be folded a second time"
assert control.out contains "untouched_elsewhere=1" else "repoint: a dated path that never folded must be left alone"
assert control.out contains "idempotent=yes" else "repoint: a second apply must change nothing"
assert control.out contains "verdict=ok" else "repoint: the control must agree with itself before it is believed"

say "GREEN: repoint -- living code repointed, dated testimony untouched, no double fold, and idempotent on a second pass."
